From 4f76b002fc29b8d52025c81c03d7e4ac36803c27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: skornuta <126527569+skornuta@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 16:30:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/27] Bindless usage feedback (VICTORY_BINDLESS_FEEDBACK=1,
 off): evict what no shader reads

The slot eviction could take none of the 3.3-3.5 GB of textures held
"idle" on the card: every one was shown by slots shaders pick by index,
and nothing on the CPU said whether a frame read them.

Translator: with the switch every texture a shader takes from the view
heap stores 1 into dword `index` of a raw buffer at the slot below the
null slot (`feedback_slot`). A plain store (every lane stores the same
value: no read-modify-write, no contention, no branch, which the handle
helpers cannot emit). Stages other than pixel and compute declare UAVs
at every stage. The setting is in the translation fingerprint.

Host (`crate::feedback`): the buffer (a dword per view heap slot, 4 MB
on a heap of 1,000,000) has its raw UAV in that slot of every view
heap, written after the heap is made null and taken out of the dynamic
slots. Every VICTORY_BINDLESS_FEEDBACK_EVERY frames (4) a list first in
a submission copies it down and clears it (COMMON -> COPY_SOURCE ->
COPY_DEST -> COMMON; the title's shaders take it from COMMON as a UAV),
into one of three read-back buffers; when the card has run it, each
slot found read gets that copy's frame.

Eviction: a texture whose slots no table shows may go once none of them
was read for VICTORY_BINDLESS_IDLE_S (45) seconds and the feedback has
watched that whole time; the 85/75 % lines and the 256 MB cap as before.
Its slots are nulled (with nothing in the air, the copy retired behind
running submissions, as before) and parked: the texture queue does not
serve them, whatever puts them in it. A slot a shader is seen reading
again is unparked and due at once, and so is one the title writes
another view into; its texture is made and uploaded again by the queue.

The pipeline library of such runs is a file of its own
(host-pipelines-feedback.bin, .next, early-pipelines-feedback.txt): the
usual library is never read, replaced or trimmed by them.

The memory CSV gets the copies landed, slots parked and slots unparked.

Tests: the store validated by dxil.dll and run on the card and on WARP
(the texture's slot reads 1, a buffer's 0, the sample unchanged); the
queue never serves a parked slot and serves it after a read or a write;
the last-seen frames and the coverage.

(cherry picked from commit 7c274de42a010033baf31ca242975c702441b7ea)
